     <section id="taxonomy"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><h2>How to Read the Field</h2><p>The repository is organized as a roadmap rather than a flat bibliography.</p></div><div class="taxonomy"><div class="tile"><h3>1. Physical model</h3><ul><li>ToF ellipsoids and light-cone transform</li><li>Wave / phasor / f-k migration</li><li>Differentiable transient rendering and TLTM iteration</li></ul></div><div class="tile"><h3>2. Acquisition regime</h3><ul><li>Dense scanning versus sparse sampling</li><li>Scannerless / real-time / active-corner systems</li><li>Motion-induced, irregular, few-shot, and single-path sampling</li></ul></div><div class="tile"><h3>3. Sensor modality</h3><ul><li>SPAD, ToF, LiDAR, camera</li><li>Radar / RF / mmWave / THz / ISAC</li><li>Acoustic, ultrasound, event camera</li></ul></div><div class="tile"><h3>4. Reconstruction target</h3><ul><li>Albedo, volume, surface, mesh</li><li>Motion, tracking, human pose</li><li>Mapping, navigation, localization</li></ul></div><div class="tile"><h3>5. Learning paradigm</h3><ul><li>CNN / transformer / Mamba / GNN</li><li>Physics-guided priors and neural operators</li><li>Neural implicit, Gaussian, and simulation tools</li></ul></div><div class="tile"><h3>6. Real-world frontier</h3><ul><li>Non-planar and limited relay surfaces</li><li>Arbitrary illumination / detection patterns</li><li>Low-cost mobile, RF, THz, metasurface, and robotic hardware</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
